{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795313427,"nonce":"VZ7lexkCCI4T3QtGBOcG0/UIDWM=","title":"Two cache-patcher GPU tests expect canvas replay to refuse a tree with no canvases","message":"`foreground_layers_cache_patchers_request_full_paint_without_mutation` and `rgba_order_primitive_cache_patchers_bail_before_mutation` (blinc_app, `#[ignore]`, need a GPU) assert `!context.redraw_canvases(\u0026tree, 160, 120)` on a tree with no canvas.\n\n68cd00c1 moved the empty-records check in `redraw_canvas_output` ahead of the ordered and foreground checks, so a tree without canvases returns \"nothing to replay\" (true) before the batch is inspected. That order is intended: with no canvas there is nothing to splice and nothing is changed. The tests predate it.\n\nBoth fail at 96cbd5d0 and at every later commit checked (a19f0b84, c36c9f6e, 7d12c971, 83e2e23e, bc8bdcea, 6441b3bf). The rest of each test checks that the cached batches are unchanged, which still holds.\n\nFix: assert replay succeeds for a tree with no canvas; keep the no-mutation checks.","files":null}]}